      "id": "ex-hh-canonical-r-matrix-for-the-double-of-cyclic-two-group",
      "concern": "The Example concludes, “Then $D(k^G)$ is a four-dimensional Hopf algebra and $R$ is its canonical quasitriangular structure.” Its functions-first basis p_x#u_g and tensor R=Σ(p_x#u_e)⊗q_x instead instantiate D(kG) under def-hh-finite-double-cross-relations and thm-hh-finite-double-hopf-structure-and-canonical-r. This is also exactly the specialization of ex-drinfeld-double-of-a-finite-group. For H=k^G, the general canonical tensor has the group-dual factor first; transporting through the natural factor flip gives the example's R21, not R. These tensors differ: the coefficient of (p_e#u_s)⊗(p_s#u_e) is 0 in R and 1 in R21. No alternative identification transporting the canonical structure is supplied. The local Hopf and quasitriangular calculations are sound, but the claimed canonical identification with D(k^G) needs adjudication.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    }
  ],
